          "quote": "AppleTalk was a proprietary suite of networking protocols developed by Apple Inc. in 1985 for Apple Macintosh computers. It was the primary protocol used by Apple devices through the 1980s and 90s. AppleTalk included features that allowed local area networks to be established ad hoc without the requirement for a centralized router or server. The AppleTalk system automatically assigned addresses, updated the distributed namespace, and configured any required inter-network routing. It was a plug-n-play system.",
          "coordinate_system": "original TXT UTF-8",
          "utf8_start": 0,
          "utf8_end": 513
        }
      ],
      "original_expected": "insufficient_evidence",
      "new_gold_active": false,
      "source_review_independent": false
